Keep recordings — DONE

1. **INFO | [RecordingArchive.kt:24](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:24).** The known fix is to keep app-only files in `getExternalFilesDir()`, write a PCM WAV header, and publish the completed file through a temporary file. Android documents [app-specific external storage](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/app-specific) and [atomic file writes](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/util/AtomicFile); Microsoft documents the [RIFF/WAV chunks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/xaudio2/resource-interchange-file-format--riff-). The draft does the storage, header, and `.part` rename steps. Its header fields are correct for the capture format and 600-second cap ([PcmAudio.kt:5](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/PcmAudio.kt:5), [RecordingArchive.kt:63](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:63)). `getExternalFilesDir()` runs when the worker calls `keep`, not on the take’s caller thread ([DictationSessionService.kt:232](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionService.kt:232), [CapturedAudioFiles.kt:26](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/CapturedAudioFiles.kt:26)). **Fix:** none for those paths. A real-file pull from the release build remains unverified; keep that phone UAT gate.

2. **HIGH | [plan:90](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/docs/feature-requests/issue-373-2026-09-25-keep-recordings.md:90), [AudioCaptureService.kt:573](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/AudioCaptureService.kt:573).** F1 identifies a real loss window but understates it. The next take sweeps the prior PCM before the queued worker necessarily opens it ([RecordingArchive.kt:25](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:25)). A delayed worker can cause this after an ordinary answer or failure, not only an instant restart after cancel. The archive silently skips a missing source, contradicting G1. **Fix:** move the closed PCM to a unique path excluded from the next-take sweep before publishing its ending; pass that path to ASR and the archive, and recover stale staged files. Add a test that holds the archive worker while the next take starts.

3. **MEDIUM | [RecordingArchive.kt:30](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:30), [RecordingArchive.kt:45](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:45).** F5 covers clock changes but misses equal-second names: sorting then follows take IDs, so it can discard a newer take. The eleventh WAV also exists between rename and prune, contrary to G2’s “at any time”; failed deletion can leave more than ten indefinitely. **Fix:** use a durable sortable order for takes, prune to nine *before* publishing the new WAV, and make failed pruning an explicit incomplete-retention result. Test eleven takes with one fixed timestamp.

4. **MEDIUM | [RecordingArchive.kt:25](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:25), [RecordingArchive.kt:29](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:29).** “Every keep first removes leftover `.part` files” is false when the source is missing; failed part deletion and a failed `listFiles` also pass silently. **Fix:** run cleanup before the source check, and treat listing or deletion failure as an archive warning while still deleting the cache file.

5. **MEDIUM | [plan:58](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/docs/feature-requests/issue-373-2026-09-25-keep-recordings.md:58), [AsrService.kt:147](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/asr/AsrService.kt:147).** The plan says ASR reads the whole file at request start. It reads the length then; `readBytes()` runs later on the recognizer worker ([AsrService.kt:159](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/asr/AsrService.kt:159)). F3’s conclusion is sound: the timeout/delete race already exists, and copying does not create an earlier delete. Other plan absolutes need correction: destroy during a speech wait *does* queue deletion ([DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1263](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1263)); there are nine listed delete sites, not ten ([plan:142](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/docs/feature-requests/issue-373-2026-09-25-keep-recordings.md:142)). F4, F6, and F7 are otherwise sound with their stated limits. **Fix:** correct those sentences and describe G1 as guaranteed only after closing F1.

6. **MEDIUM | [RecordingArchiveTest.kt:32](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchiveTest.kt:32), [CapturedAudioFilesTest.kt:65](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/CapturedAudioFilesTest.kt:65).** By inspection, the assertions would reject the named raw-copy, wrong-name, no-prune, null-folder, wrong-order, thrown-archive, and no-part-cleanup mutations. No mutation was run in this read-only review, so **RED is unproven**. The WAV test also omits the `fmt ` ID, format length, block alignment, and total-length oracle; none of these tests catches F1 or equal-second pruning. **Fix:** assert the complete literal 44-byte header and file length, add the two race/order cases above, then run each named mutation and record its failing test.

